@startuml
mainframe ticketing checkin at entry of venue

actor Customer
actor Attendant
participant orderEndpoint
participant eventEndpoint

group display the ticket token (QR code)  [token is in JWT format]
Customer --> orderEndpoint: GET /orders
Customer --> orderEndpoint: GET /orders/{orderId}
Customer --> orderEndpoint: POST /orders/{orderId}/token
note over Customer, orderEndpoint
seatId shall be supplied when applying token, 
as one order can contain multiple seats
end note


end

group checkin for specified event and session
Attendant --> eventEndpoint: GET /events/{eventId}
Attendant --> eventEndpoint: GET /events/{eventId}/sessions
Attendant --> eventEndpoint: GET /events/{eventId}/sessions/{sessionId}
Attendant --> Customer: Scan the QR code for token


Attendant --> eventEndpoint: POST /events/{eventId}/sessions/{sessionId}
note over Attendance, eventEndpoint
Supply token, event and session to the service for checkin
System will check the JWT timestamp for token expiration
Upon successful checking in, checkinTimestamp of corresponding seat will be updated.
end note


Customer --> orderEndpoint: GET /orders/{orderId}
note over Customer, orderEndpoint
refer to Order.seats.checkinTimeStamp in returned payload
end note

end




@enduml